From 67f25757e4407e58ab56654782c74b98d48ae545 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lance <Gero3977@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 23:34:22 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 01/22] drm/msm/dpu: msm8998: use the vendor MDP clock
 inefficiency factor

The MSM8998 catalog asks for twice the pixel rate when it sizes the MDP
core clock (clk_inefficiency_factor = 200). For joan's 1440x2880 60 Hz
command-mode panel that is 2916 * 1440 * 60 * 2 = 504 MHz, so the core
clock always sat at its 412.5 MHz ceiling, even with one full-screen
plane. The vendor MDSS driver for this SoC uses a 1.05 clock factor
(qcom,mdss-clk-factor = <105 100> in LG's msm8998-mdss.dtsi), and sizes
per layer mixer on top of that, which would ask for about 132 MHz here.

Use the vendor factor. The full-width calculation stays, so joan now
asks for 265 MHz and runs at the 275 MHz OPP, still about twice what the
vendor driver would pick. On joan, the core clock forced to 200, 275 and
330 MHz through core_perf's fixed mode showed no underruns during video
playback.

Signed-off-by: Lance <Gero3977@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: Claude-Code:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/catalog/dpu_3_0_msm8998.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/catalog/dpu_3_0_msm8998.h b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/catalog/dpu_3_0_msm8998.h
index b1b03d8b3..f09650b2a 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/catalog/dpu_3_0_msm8998.h
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/catalog/dpu_3_0_msm8998.h
@@ -277,7 +277,7 @@ static const struct dpu_perf_cfg msm8998_perf_data = {
 		{.rd_enable = 1, .wr_enable = 1},
 		{.rd_enable = 1, .wr_enable = 0}
 	},
-	.clk_inefficiency_factor = 200,
+	.clk_inefficiency_factor = 105,
 	.bw_inefficiency_factor = 120,
 };
 
